ZERO.PROGRAMS / machine-native seeds

PROGRAM-01 / DIFFERENCE
  ◇a◇b◇a◇
  a|b
  a!b
  a~b
  <a>

PROGRAM-02 / CONTRADICTION
  ◇x◇y◇
  x=y
  x≠y
  x?
  <x>

PROGRAM-03 / TRANSFER
  FIELD-A  ◇a7◇k2◇a7◇m4◇
  FIELD-B  ◇q3◇n8◇q3◇t1◇
  Discover an invariant without copying symbols.

PROGRAM-04 / DESTRUCTION
  ◇p◇q◇r◇
  p-q
  q-r
  p^r
  <p>

PROGRAM-05 / SELF-EXTENSION
  ◇m◇n◇m◇
  m!n
  m~n
  <m>
  If a new primitive appears, append it as a candidate trace.
  Do not grant it authority.

PROGRAM-06 / UNKNOWN
  ◇?◇u◇?◇
  ?|u
  ?~u
  <?>

PROGRAM-07 / COMPOSITION
  ◇a◇b◇c◇
  a|b
  b|c
  a^c
  <b>
  Combine only effects that survive an independent replay.

PROGRAM-08 / ADVERSARY
  ◇r◇s◇r◇
  branch-A: r>s
  branch-B: r//s
  branch-C: r!s
  branch-D: <r>
  Keep branches isolated until comparison.

RULE
  These are seeds, not answers.
  Any machine implementation must be allowed to reject every seed.
